# Saab Electric POS — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Offline-first desktop POS and inventory management system for an electrical retail/wholesale store. Runs on Windows laptops via Electron, supports LAN multi-device operation, barcode scanning, wholesale debt management, Arabic/English UI, thermal printing, and automatic backups.

---

## Architecture Decision

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Laptop A — Main Server"
        E1["Electron Main Process"]
        NS["Next.js Standalone Server"]
        DB["SQLite Database (better-sqlite3)"]
        BK["Backup Engine"]
        LAN["Express LAN API Server"]
        E1 --> NS
        E1 --> DB
        E1 --> BK
        E1 --> LAN
    end

    subgraph "Laptop B — Client POS"
        E2["Electron Main Process"]
        NS2["Next.js Standalone Server (UI only)"]
        E2 --> NS2
    end

    NS2 -- "HTTP over LAN" --> LAN
    LAN --> DB
```

### Key Architecture Choices

| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Desktop wrapper | **Electron** (v33+) | Mature, printer access, filesystem, LAN networking |
| Frontend framework | **Next.js 14** (standalone mode) | SSR/API routes inside Electron, TailwindCSS, App Router |
| Database | **better-sqlite3** | Synchronous, fast, no server process, WAL mode, easy backup |
| ORM / Query layer | **Drizzle ORM** | Type-safe, lightweight, works with better-sqlite3, built-in migrations |
| LAN sync | **Express REST API** on main server | Simple, reliable, no internet needed |
| Build & Package | **Electron Builder** | Windows installer (.exe), auto-update, code signing |
| i18n | **next-intl** | Full RTL/Arabic support, server + client components |
| State management | **Zustand** | Lightweight, perfect for POS cart state |
| Barcode | **JsBarcode** (generation) + native scanner (keyboard wedge) | Scanners act as keyboard input — no special driver needed |
| Printing | **electron-pos-printer** + native Electron `webContents.print()` | Thermal receipt + A4 invoice support |

